# 01.2.1-T2: what prettier --check must not touch.

# Build output / caches
node_modules
**/dist
**/bin
**/obj
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.husky/_

# Lock files — regenerated by the package managers, never hand-formatted
package-lock.json
**/packages.lock.json

# Planning documents: prose is not prettier-formatted
plans/**
# docs/source is generated plan tooling output; ADRs are authored markdown
docs/**

# Root planning/status docs
DECISIONS.md
RECOMMENDATIONS.md
SESSION-SUMMARY.md
STATUS.md
AGENTS.md

# 01.3.2-T4.1: the RFC 8785 reference vectors are byte-exact input/output pairs
# (the expected canonical form is compared as bytes), never reformatted. They live
# in fixtures/ because the xUnit suite and the CLI Vitest suite both assert them.
# The README next to them stays prettier-checked.
fixtures/rfc8785/input
fixtures/rfc8785/output

# 01.3.2-T1.1: `packages/sdk/gen` is generated by @hey-api/openapi-ts — byte-exact output
# of a pinned generator, never reformatted (same rule as fixtures/rfc8785 above).
# The handwritten `packages/sdk/src` stays prettier-checked.
packages/sdk/gen

# 01.6.1-T3.2: a fixture's expected.json IS the RFC 8785 canonical byte sequence
# (packages/test-fixtures/src/goldenFile.ts compares it as bytes, like
# rfc8785/output above), so prettier must never reflow it.
**/fixtures/**/expected.json

# 01.3.2-T2.3: parity-corpus vectors that must stay byte-exact — the cap
# vectors are compact single-line JSON near the 1 MiB limit, and
